# *** THIS FIXTURE IS DERIVED, NOT OBSERVED. ***
#
# EXPECTED VERDICT: FAIL.
# It is `pass-observed-vacuous-pairing` with ONE character span changed: DISC
# 43's LAYOUT name `Net 25087` becomes `Net X99/6106`, the real layout-path
# form Calibre prints for an unnamed net inside an instance (taken verbatim
# from the rzG report, DISC 62). Nothing else differs.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES: the vacuous-pairing rule is NOT an amnesty for zero-overlap
# discrepancies. It withdraws the SOURCE name and re-resolves the entry by the
# LAYOUT name - the same fallback the gate has always used for an unpaired net
# - so a vacuous pair whose layout name IS a hierarchy path is STILL a sub-top
# finding. A widening that returned `top` unconditionally would pass this arm,
# and that mutation (M11) is what this arm catches.
#



